# The initializer stores null into owner and the caller of the constructor overwrites it at once. The cell is born with the final value: one store a field.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="adopt" role=ResultWrapper
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Int64, Int64 b@[[fields]] = Patchpoint({{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[name]] = Extract(b@[[fields]], <<0,
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[owner]] = Extract(b@[[fields]], <<1,
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[item]] = Patchpoint(${{*}}(b@{{*}}):Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), {{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[name]], b@[[item]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[owner]], b@[[item]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK: Return(b@[[item]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The store behind the construction is no store of its own: it has no write barrier and no test of the shape.
# NONE-LABEL: name="adopt" role=ResultWrapper
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSCell
# NONE-NOT: :PutSlot
# NONE-NOT: :WriteBarrier
# NONE-COUNT-2: Store(
# NONE-NOT: Store(
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
